{"key":"enterprise/T1569.002","id":"T1569.002","name":"Service Execution","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1569","tactics":["execution"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse the Windows service control manager to execute malicious commands or payloads. The Windows service control manager (services.exe) is an interface to manage and manipulate services. The service control manager is accessible to users via GUI components as well as system utilities such as sc.exe and Net. PsExec can also be used to execute commands or payloads via a temporary Windows service created through the service control…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1569/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--f1951e8a-500e-4a26-8803-76d95c4554b4","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.723Z","source_object_version":"1.3","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0060","name":"Service Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0060","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5297a638-1382-4f0c-8472-0d21830bf705","page":"telemetry/DC0060/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0421","name":"Detection Strategy for System Services Service Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0421","stix_id":"